            <ArticleTitle>Speeding the dissemination and implementation of evidence-based interventions for cancer control and prevention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>261-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite the growing menu of evidence-based interventions to prevent and control cancer, such interventions continue to be underused in practice. This commentary describes interactive approaches to speeding the dissemination and implementation of evidence-based interventions and illustrates these approaches using examples from obesity prevention and tobacco control.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
